       "en": "on WATER. On Paxos, ask about the cisterns, about the price per cubic meter in August, about who decides the priority between hotels and households. Scarcity is the best revealer of social structure that exists: when a resource stops being sufficient, its distribution reveals the real rule. It is the same ethnography you would carry out in a settlement in Lima with a cistern and a water-tanker truck, and the comparison is not a whim: in both cases, the water market is where real citizenship can be read."
