       "en": "Third, an exercise for Paxos. The Nazca puquios and the Paxiot cisterns solve the same problem with different solutions in comparable eras. When you see the cisterns and the terraced olive groves, think in terms of INFRASTRUCTURE OF SCARCITY: what institutions are needed to build and maintain something like this, who administers them, and what happens when the logic that sustained them — small community, controlled consumption, obligatory reciprocity — is replaced by a seasonal demand ten times greater and non-negotiable. The answer to that question is, today, the central conflict of the Ionian islands, and it is the same question any high-Andean community asks itself when facing a mining project."
