     "en": "The next entrega closes Block II with the figure who made 1821 possible without meaning to: Ali Pasha of Ioannina, the warlord who ruled Epirus as a state of his own facing Corfu, negotiated as an equal with Napoleon and with the British, and whose destruction by the sultan left the empire without troops to spare just as the revolution broke out."
