       "en": "In Athens, Syntagma Square, where on December 3, 1944, gunfire was opened on the demonstration: there is a discreet plaque. And the National Museum of Contemporary Art or the Benaki Museum usually hold material from the period. If you have time and stomach for it, the Kaisarianí neighborhood, a historic stronghold of the Athenian left, settled by refugees of 1923 and punished in 1944 and afterward: today it is an ordinary neighborhood with a very dense memory."
