       "en": "In Corfu and Paxos, this period had less intensity than on the mainland: the civil war was chiefly a phenomenon of the mountains of the north and center. That relative unscathedness is itself a datum, and it helps explain why Ionian politics historically had a different profile from that of Epirus or Macedonia."
